{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-352528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨5{t}^{4}+3,\\,\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$\n\n$v=⟨${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{4}+3),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨20{t}^{3},-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "972600df0dffcfaef07aafeba28ce4b275ca8b2195529bf6eb8b68c636aa406a"} {"question" "q-352528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20t^3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352528" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352528" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{4}{t^3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-121714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},2-5t⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-121714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{{t}^{2}-1}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-5t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-121714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "972600df0dffcfaef07aafeba28ce4b275ca8b2195529bf6eb8b68c636aa406a"} {"question" "q-121714" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-121714" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "v=⟨2t{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},-5⟩"] ["math" "v=⟨2t{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},2⟩"] ["math" "v=⟨t{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},-5⟩"] ["math" "v=⟨{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},-5⟩"] ["math" "v=⟨{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-121714" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "v=⟨2t{e}^{{t}^{2}-1},-5⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-121715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨1-3{t}^{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1)⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-121715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-3{t}^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6t,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-121715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "972600df0dffcfaef07aafeba28ce4b275ca8b2195529bf6eb8b68c636aa406a"} {"question" "q-121715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-121715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "v=⟨-6,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)⟩"] ["math" "v=⟨-6,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)⟩"] ["math" "v=⟨-6t,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)⟩"] ["math" "v=⟨-6t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)⟩"] ["math" "v=⟨-6t,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-121715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "v=⟨-6t,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-31637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ is moving in the $x$-$y$ plane. Its position vector relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{3/2}+4{t}^{2},\\,11t-1⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-31637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3/2}+4{t}^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(11t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t}+8t,\\,11⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-31637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "972600df0dffcfaef07aafeba28ce4b275ca8b2195529bf6eb8b68c636aa406a"} {"question" "q-31637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-31637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "v=⟨\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t}+4t,\\,10⟩"] ["math" "v=⟨\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t}+8t,\\,11⟩"] ["math" "v=⟨\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{3/2}+8{t}^{2},\\,11t⟩"] ["math" "v=⟨\\sqrt{t}+4t,\\,11t⟩"] ["math" "v=⟨\\sqrt{t}+4t,\\,11⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-31637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "v=⟨\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t}+8t,\\,11⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ is moving in the $x$-$y$ plane. Its position vector relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v.$\n\n$v=⟨${{field-1}}$\\,,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "972600df0dffcfaef07aafeba28ce4b275ca8b2195529bf6eb8b68c636aa406a"} {"question" "q-352544" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352544" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6\\cos(2t)+5\\sin(t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\frac{7}{t+1},\\,\\frac{5t}{{t}^{2}+1}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=2.$ Do not round the answers.\n\n$v(2)=⟨${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{7}{t+1}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{5t}{{t}^{2}+1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{7}{(t+1)^{2}},\\frac{5-5{t}^{2}}{({t}^{2}+1)^{2}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2,$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =⟨-\\frac{7}{(2+1)^{2}},\\,\\frac{5-5(2)^{2}}{((2)^{2}+1)^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{7}{9},\\,-\\frac{3}{5}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "972600df0dffcfaef07aafeba28ce4b275ca8b2195529bf6eb8b68c636aa406a"} {"question" "q-352549" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352549" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{7}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352549" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-352549" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-347187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨7{t}^{2},\\,-18⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=5.$ Do not round the answers.\n\n$v(5)=⟨${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-347187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7{t}^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-18)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨14t,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=5,$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(5) & =⟨14(5),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨70,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/state.json" "file_sha256" "aa7bd7c741e5c3deb397050d8b46a3549627aaed0824252feb040909ac051c8f"} {"question" "q-347187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040567/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "972600df0dffcfaef